To edit the **"Supply Chains"** option in your **Government Dashboard**, you can modify both the **HTML** (to update the menu option) and the **CSS** (to adjust its styling if necessary).

Here’s how you can edit the **"Supply Chains"** option in the dashboard:

### 1. **Update the HTML for the "Supply Chains" Option**

If you want to edit the label of the "Supply Chains" option or link it to a different section or page, you can adjust the `<a>` tag inside the sidebar.

#### Example: Update the "Supply Chains" Option
Let's say you want to rename the option to "Supply Chain Management" and link it to a specific page, like `supply_chain.html`.

#### **Updated HTML:**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Government Dashboard</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>

<header>
    <div class="logo">Pandemic Resilience System</div>
</header>

<div class="sidebar">
    <div class="title">Pandemic Resilience</div>
    <a href="#">Dashboard</a>
    <a href="#">Vaccination Tracking</a>
    <a href="supply_chain.html" id="supplyChainLink">Supply Chain Management</a> <!-- Edited option here -->
    <a href="#">Reports</a>
</div>

<div class="main-content">
    <div class="box">
        <h2>Supply Chain Overview</h2>
        <!-- Content goes here -->
    </div>
    <div class="stats">
        <!-- Stats content goes here -->
    </div>
    <div class="graph">
        <p>Graph Placeholder</p>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### Key Changes in the HTML:
1. **Renamed Option**: The label for the "Supply Chains" option has been updated to **"Supply Chain Management"**.
2. **Link Change**: The link now points to `supply_chain.html`. You can change this to point to a specific page or section as needed.

---

### 2. **Edit the CSS for the "Supply Chain" Option (Optional)**

If you want to apply custom styles specifically to this option (for instance, changing its color, adding hover effects, or making it standout), you can target the `a` tag with the `id="supplyChainLink"`.

#### **CSS Update:**

```css
/* Sidebar styling */
.sidebar {
  width: 250px;
  background-color: #2f2f2f;
  position: fixed;
  height: 100%;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  padding-top: 20px;
}

.sidebar .title {
  color: white;
  font-size: 2rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-align: left;
